Possibly one of the most tear-jerking games I have ever played in my entire life. The beautiful 8k resolution, 60 fps this game can run in really shows the depth the games developers put in. I mean, this game could beat any triple A titles any day. Grand Theft Auto Five? Nah, bad rats has a better storyline. Half Life 2? Nah, this game has better graphics, and better physics. Any Valve game? No thank you. When you beat this game, you will have clinical depression. Honestly, the way this game messes with your mind, its revolutionary.
//// Pros \\\\
-Pretty much every part of this game
//// Cons \\\\
-Non existant

What you should know about this game in three painless steps:
1) It's free;
2) it will take about 15 minuites of your time;
3) If you have a soul, you will like it.
Writing any more would just spoil the fun.

Part Fire emblem part Clannad. This game is what set the bar for a great visual novel. The strategy portions of the game actually will effect the outcome of the story, and the interplay of the story and strategy make you pretty invested into the troops. It isn't some generic spirit mook you are fighting with it is the cute and shy Hellion, and knowing about her makes you sad if you can't bring her home safe ;;
The one thing I would say as a complaint is some of the missions are too damn long, which is ok for a pure strategy game but as the whole game is pretty much one long war campaign it seems like the missions that are super long could have been subdivided into smaller tasks with story breaking it up. Now there are some that sorta do that... kinda... but it stays in the strategy mode engine which doesn't let you save when they are talking and only gives the profile icons for people talking so it isn't as immersive as the visual novel mode engine, which has voice acting and quick saving.
Anyway. The game is great. if you like visual novels or strategy games like fireemblem or super robot wars, this is a must.

I purchased this game at full price the week before promotion. And in the following week, I played for nearly 60 hrs. This is a really fantastic game, it is turn-based, and lots of interaction with the environment. You can probably kill boss in numerous creative ways! Quests are interesting and lots of modern humors inside.
Pros:
Strategic Caculation;
Dynamic Environment;
Funny Dialogue;
Full voice;
Interaction with animals!
Cons:
It's slow, very slow;
Performs badly on Macbook;
Heavy on texts, so better to be patient;
Overall:
Recommend!

